{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB12141 - MONDO_grouped_18874_4643",
  "verbalization": "Gilteritinib, a multitargeted tyrosine kinase inhibitor, is associated with the indication of Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With or Without Maturation, both of which are classified under Myeloid Leukemia. The evidence suggests that Gilteritinib may be repurposed for the treatment of Myeloid Leukemia, as it is linked to Mitoxantrone, a drug known to be effective in treating Myeloid Leukemia. The shared indication between Gilteritinib and Mitoxantrone, along with the classification of Acute Myeloid Leukemia under Myeloid Leukemia, supports a potential mechanistic link between the two entities. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Gilteritinib to Myeloid Leukemia through Mitoxantrone indicates a possible role in the treatment of this disease. The integration of these pathways suggests that Gilteritinib may exert its therapeutic effects through mechanisms that are relevant to the pathophysiology of Myeloid Leukemia, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
